The pure-private minimax absolute risk over \(\mathcal P_K\) is
\[
R_{n,\epsilon}^{\mathrm{DP},K}
=\inf_{T_{\mathrm{DP}}:\,\epsilon\text{-DP under }\sim_1}
\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_K}
\mathbb E_{P^{\otimes n},T_{\mathrm{DP}}}
\left|T_{\mathrm{DP}}(D_n)-\theta(P)\right|,
\]
where every kernel has domain \(\mathcal O^n\), output space \([-2,2]\), and replacement adjacency \(\sim_1\).  Thus \(R_{n,\epsilon}^{\mathrm{DP},K}\in[0,2]\); the upper endpoint follows from the admissible constant-zero kernel and \(\theta(P)\in[-2,2]\).
